<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laguna de Términos</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Laguna de Términos is a large coastal lagoon in the Mexican state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a>, separated from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a> by the island of Carmen. It was named by Spanish explorers in 1518. Rivers including the Candelaria flow into it, and in Maya times it was a hub of the canoe trade on the routes around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán Peninsula</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laguna-de-terminos.jpg" alt="Laguna de Términos" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Earth Observatory images by Joshua Stevens, using Landsat data from the U.S. Geological Survey. Story by Kathryn Hansen. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laguna_de_T%C3%A9rminos.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
